    <string name="common_settings_max_suggested_tags">Default max suggested tags per document</string>
    <string name="common_settings_max_suggested_tags_help">Default number of tags the assistant proposes per document (%1$d-%2$d); can be changed per run on the AI tagging page.</string>
    <string name="common_settings_max_new_tags">Default max new tags per document</string>
    <string name="common_settings_max_new_tags_help">Default number of brand-new tags (not already in your library) the assistant may propose per document (%1$d-%2$d; 0 = never); can be changed per run on the AI tagging page.</string>
    <string name="common_settings_ai_auto_on_ocr">Tag and fill in new documents automatically</string>
    <string name="common_settings_ai_auto_on_ocr_help">Right after a document is scanned or imported and its text is read, the assistant applies tags from your existing tags (it never creates new ones) and fills in every field marked "Let AI fill this in" when it is still empty. Applied without review, so each new document costs one request.</string>
    <string name="common_settings_ai_ocr_auto">Read text with the assistant instead of on-device OCR</string>
    <string name="common_settings_ai_ocr_auto_help">Uses the model to read every scanned page, which handles handwriting, tables and faint scans far better than on-device OCR. This costs one request per page, not per document, and it also re-reads documents that on-device OCR already handled. Documents longer than %1$d pages keep using on-device OCR here; you can still ask for those one at a time. Leave this off to read text on-device and use "Read text with assistant" on individual documents instead.</string>

    <string name="common_settings_ai_test">Test this setup</string>
    <string name="common_settings_ai_test_help">Checks three things in turn: that the server answers, that the model replies to a question, and that it can read text off a page image. Costs two very small requests. Checking stops at the first failure, since everything after it would fail for the same reason.</string>
